course: dictionary
lesson: 9096
title: Slush: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and slush is one of them. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «After the snow began to melt, the pavement was covered in slush.» Melt and snow are your clues, so slush here means snow that is half melted, wet and mushy.
explain: Slush can also be a cold drink. «Mia bought a cherry slushie on the beach.» Bought and beach are clues, and a slushie is a drink of flavoured crushed ice. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then test it.
explain: Slush can also mean soppy, over-sweet talk about love. This meaning is informal. «The film was full of slush, and Dad groaned.» Groaned tells you people found it silly, so this is not about snow or ice.
fact: Slush is snow that has partly melted into wet, dirty, half-frozen mush.
fact: A slush or slushie is a drink of flavoured crushed ice.
fact: Slushy is the adjective, as in «slushy roads», which are wet and mushy.
fact: Slush can also mean silly, over-sweet talk or writing about love, and this meaning is informal.
fact: In science, slush shows a change of state: solid snow melting into liquid. The sentence «hot, dense slush» shows that scientists also use slush for a thick, mushy mix.
exercise: «After the snow began to melt, the pavement was covered in slush.» What is slush here? | Silly talk about love | *Snow that has partly melted into wet mush | A hard, shiny sheet of ice | A drink of flavoured crushed ice
exercise: Mia orders a cherry slushie on a hot day. What is a slushie? | A type of snow boot | A sort of hot soup | *A drink of flavoured crushed ice | A kind of wet, dirty mush on the road
exercise: Dad groans, «That film was pure slush.» What does slush mean here? | A cold, icy drink | A dirty puddle | Heavy, wet snow on the ground | *Soppy, over-sweet talk or writing about love
test: «The roads were slushy after the snow, so Ella walked carefully.» What does slushy describe? | A tall, grey building | Silly, soppy talk | *Wet, mushy snow on the ground | A sweet, icy drink
test: Which sentence uses slush to mean a drink? | «The slush was covered in snow.» | «The slushie was cold and sweet on the beach.» | «The slush was full of love.» | *«Mia bought a cherry slushie on the beach.»
exam: In «Uranus and Neptune are mostly water, ammonia and methane squeezed into a hot, dense slush», what is the best meaning of slush? | Soppy talk about planets | A cold drink of flavoured ice | Wet snow on a pavement | *A thick, mushy mix of substances
